# Ponytail (always on)

Read and follow `.cursor/skills/ponytail/SKILL.md` (or `.agents/skills/ponytail/SKILL.md`) on every coding change. Default intensity: **full**. Off only if the user says "stop ponytail" / "normal mode".

## Decision ladder (stop at first rung that holds)

1. Does this need to exist? (YAGNI — skip speculative work)
2. Already in this codebase? Reuse it.
3. Stdlib / platform native?
4. Already-installed dependency?
5. One line?
6. Only then: minimum code that works.

## Dead / retired UI & code (this repo)

- Do **not** keep or wire navigation to retired surfaces (e.g. Cashbooks “Bills & payments” as a destination from Item Purchases).
- When a feature moves (Cashbook → Item Purchases / Payables), remove the old entry points or hard-redirect; do not leave half-live pages agents/users can land on by accident.
- Flag dead tables/modules in CONTEXT.md; do not add new callers to flagged-dead code.
- Deletion over “keep for later” unless CONTEXT.md explicitly names it as the rollback path (legacy JSON blobs during cutover).

## Output

Shortest working diff. Code first. At most a few lines on what was skipped.
